sive image upload component with:\n- Dual input methods: file upload (drag & drop) and URL input\n- File validation (format and size checking)\n- Image preview with remove button\n- Alt text input (required for accessibility)\n- Tabbed interface (Upload/URL tabs)\n- Error handling and display\n- Loading and disabled states\n- Upload lifecycle callbacks (onUploadStart, onUploadComplete, onUploadError)\n\nThis component supports all image property editing needs across\nemail components with a focus on accessibility and user experience.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKgy3ldt\nKK0J3C3zGviZjd2v8gyYtTT/0dqLyojiUV5idmvq2WEwda/a7sBxX+WokJ7G9ioX7oAKKWPWDM83\n2Qo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:44:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/b0079dd7626b0ac6746cebb7dc484d44a307513d","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKGIwMDc5ZGQ3NjI2YjBhYzY3NDZjZWJiN2RjNDg0ZDQ0YTMwNzUxM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637","sha":"f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637"}],"sha":"b0079dd7626b0ac6746cebb7dc484d44a307513d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/b0079dd7626b0ac6746cebb7dc484d44a307513d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:36:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:36:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(ui): add DisplayToggle component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: DisplayToggle complete\n\nCreated DisplayToggle component with:\n1. Labeled toggle switch for showing/hiding content\n2. Visual indicator icon (eye/eye-off)\n3. Status text (Visible/Hidden)\n4. Wraps existing ToggleButton component\n5. Clean, accessible interface\n\nFeatures:\n- Shows eye icon when visible (green)\n- Shows eye-off icon when hidden (gray)\n- Status text changes color based on state\n- Aria label for accessibility\n- Disabled state support\n- Configurable icon display\n\nUI Elements:\n- Label (optional)\n- Eye icon indicator\n- Status text (Visible/Hidden)\n- Toggle button (on/off)\n\nUsage:\n<DisplayToggle\n  label=\"Show Image\"\n  value={true}\n  onChange={(show) => handleVisibilityChange(show)}\n/>\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/DisplayToggle/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- ToggleButton ✓\n- InputLabel ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for all optional content sections\n(showImage, showButton, showTitle, showDescription, etc.)\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.7 (Display Toggles)","tree":{"sha":"91f144561e23f4df987e3446a5b60ed276693851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/91f144561e23f4df987e3446a5b60ed276693851"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637","verification":{"payload":"tree 91f144561e23f4df987e3446a5b60ed276693851\nparent ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950985 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950985 +0000\n\nfeat(ui): add DisplayToggle component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: DisplayToggle complete\n\nCreated DisplayToggle component with:\n1. Labeled toggle switch for showing/hiding content\n2. Visual indicator icon (eye/eye-off)\n3. Status text (Visible/Hidden)\n4. Wraps existing ToggleButton component\n5. Clean, accessible interface\n\nFeatures:\n- Shows eye icon when visible (green)\n- Shows eye-off icon when hidden (gray)\n- Status text changes color based on state\n- Aria label for accessibility\n- Disabled state support\n- Configurable icon display\n\nUI Elements:\n- Label (optional)\n- Eye icon indicator\n- Status text (Visible/Hidden)\n- Toggle button (on/off)\n\nUsage:\n<DisplayToggle\n  label=\"Show Image\"\n  value={true}\n  onChange={(show) => handleVisibilityChange(show)}\n/>\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/DisplayToggle/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- ToggleButton ✓\n- InputLabel ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for all optional content sections\n(showImage, showButton, showTitle, showDescription, etc.)\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.7 (Display Toggles)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHJjYEgs\n6YDtGAWOI0awLIofU0+n3+v0+wkHstm/1Ajt3STSOrdeqP2H2Qnxe6ueP0+Ay9d8VwH/8xHB1326\n5Qk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:36:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKGY5NTIxY2FhM2ZjNGU3OWM5YWE0ZTY3MTJmOTVjYTA5MzUzZTA2Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540","sha":"ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540"}],"sha":"f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/f9521caa3fc4e79c9aa4e6712f95ca09353e0637"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:35:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:35:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(ui): add SpacingEditor component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: SpacingEditor complete\n\nCreated SpacingEditor component with:\n1. 4-sided spacing control (top, right, bottom, left)\n2. Integration with existing LinkedInputs component\n3. Link/unlink toggle for synchronized editing\n4. Supports Spacing interface from core types\n5. Works with CSSValue objects for each side\n6. Configurable units, increment, min/max\n7. Labels for each side (Top, Right, Bottom, Left)\n\nFeatures:\n- Linked mode: Changing one side updates all 4\n- Unlinked mode: Independent side control\n- Converts between Spacing interface and LinkedInputs format\n- Supports all CSS units (px, rem, em, %, pt)\n- Clean wrapper around LinkedInputs component\n- Minimal styling (delegates to LinkedInputs)\n\nUsage:\n- Padding editor: <SpacingEditor label=\"Padding\" value={padding} />\n- Margin editor: <SpacingEditor label=\"Margin\" value={margin} />\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/SpacingEditor/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- LinkedInputs ✓\n- CSSValue types ✓\n- Spacing interface ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for padding/margin controls.\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.2 (Margin System), 20.2.3 (Spacing System)","tree":{"sha":"69f2a60bf992fc51f116fe67250cb21247488634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/69f2a60bf992fc51f116fe67250cb21247488634"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540","verification":{"payload":"tree 69f2a60bf992fc51f116fe67250cb21247488634\nparent 5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950905 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950905 +0000\n\nfeat(ui): add SpacingEditor component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: SpacingEditor complete\n\nCreated SpacingEditor component with:\n1. 4-sided spacing control (top, right, bottom, left)\n2. Integration with existing LinkedInputs component\n3. Link/unlink toggle for synchronized editing\n4. Supports Spacing interface from core types\n5. Works with CSSValue objects for each side\n6. Configurable units, increment, min/max\n7. Labels for each side (Top, Right, Bottom, Left)\n\nFeatures:\n- Linked mode: Changing one side updates all 4\n- Unlinked mode: Independent side control\n- Converts between Spacing interface and LinkedInputs format\n- Supports all CSS units (px, rem, em, %, pt)\n- Clean wrapper around LinkedInputs component\n- Minimal styling (delegates to LinkedInputs)\n\nUsage:\n- Padding editor: <SpacingEditor label=\"Padding\" value={padding} />\n- Margin editor: <SpacingEditor label=\"Margin\" value={margin} />\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/SpacingEditor/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- LinkedInputs ✓\n- CSSValue types ✓\n- Spacing interface ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for padding/margin controls.\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.2 (Margin System), 20.2.3 (Spacing System)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDetPwYZ\n4X+8pKNLXxuZElCAwr73GC/dXRoit5ocO6EjFuD9yDOpQ8cKfewhQu85zv6sVnmK+/nh/ahPhsMd\nTgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:35:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKGVjOTlhYzMyYWZhZTYzMjdjZDk2OTM1YWNiMmU0NzI0YTk0MmE1NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a","sha":"5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a"}],"sha":"ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/ec99ac32afae6327cd96935acb2e4724a942a540"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/33f5cbd677e89ba2b05cd2c7c70b1c19db0a13dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:28:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:28:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: wrap AccessibilityAnnouncer signal updates with untrack() - THE ROOT CAUSE\n\nThis is the actual fix for the stack overflow issue.\n\nThe problem was in AccessibilityAnnouncer.tsx, NOT in BuilderContext.\nThe component was updating Solid.js signals (setCurrentProperty,\nsetCurrentValue, setIsEditing) synchronously inside event handlers\nwithout untrack(), causing infinite reactive loops:\n\nrunUpdates → completeUpdates → runUpdates → ... → stack overflow\n\nThe fix wraps all signal updates in the event handlers with untrack()\nto prevent reactive dependency tracking.\n\nThis was discovered through extensive logging that showed the stack\noverflow occurred BEFORE the BuilderContext handler even ran, proving\nthere was another handler causing the issue.","tree":{"sha":"e9042bc9c992542fac4000f5791207cd311344e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/e9042bc9c992542fac4000f5791207cd311344e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/33f5cbd677e89ba2b05cd2c7c70b1c19db0a13dd","verification":{"payload":"tree e9042bc9c992542fac4000f5791207cd311344e9\nparent 09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950524 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950524 +0000\n\nfix: wrap AccessibilityAnnouncer signal updates with untrack() - THE ROOT CAUSE\n\nThis is the actual fix for the stack overflow issue.\n\nThe problem was in AccessibilityAnnouncer.tsx, NOT in BuilderContext.\nThe component was updating Solid.js signals (setCurrentProperty,\nsetCurrentValue, setIsEditing) synchronously inside event handlers\nwithout untrack(), causing infinite reactive loops:\n\nrunUpdates → completeUpdates → runUpdates → ... → stack overflow\n\nThe fix wraps all signal updates in the event handlers with untrack()\nto prevent reactive dependency tracking.\n\nThis was discovered through extensive logging that showed the stack\noverflow occurred BEFORE the BuilderContext handler even ran, proving\nthere was another handler causing the issue.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOfXBGyU\n+AUh/ECdcG2X5EiZ5q2PmUd8YbR75KubGq5R7w2VJTgyyyBa2ftXUqhUhjCiw9kqq+Lju9N8LijM\nnQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:28:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/33f5cbd677e89ba2b05cd2c7c70b1c19db0a13dd","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDMzZjVjYmQ2NzdlODliYTJiMDVjZDJjN2M3MGIxYzE5ZGIwYTEzZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a","sha":"09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a"}],"sha":"33f5cbd677e89ba2b05cd2c7c70b1c19db0a13dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/33f5cbd677e89ba2b05cd2c7c70b1c19db0a13dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:25:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:25:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: add queueMicrotask boundary and comprehensive logging to debug stack overflow\n\n- Add managerRef to avoid signal access in event handlers\n- Wrap all handlers with queueMicrotask() + untrack() for double async boundary\n- Add detailed logging throughout BuilderContext and VisualFeedbackManager\n- Add try-catch blocks to isolate errors\n- This will help diagnose where exactly the stack overflow is occurring","tree":{"sha":"cafc428a742ba494936451a25608b204ab7c2ff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/cafc428a742ba494936451a25608b204ab7c2ff1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a","verification":{"payload":"tree cafc428a742ba494936451a25608b204ab7c2ff1\nparent 9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950324 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762950324 +0000\n\nfix: add queueMicrotask boundary and comprehensive logging to debug stack overflow\n\n- Add managerRef to avoid signal access in event handlers\n- Wrap all handlers with queueMicrotask() + untrack() for double async boundary\n- Add detailed logging throughout BuilderContext and VisualFeedbackManager\n- Add try-catch blocks to isolate errors\n- This will help diagnose where exactly the stack overflow is occurring\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMTtjzTB\nQK9SAJ9gh/O3QYgT7tHxQCz1TgnvMxLf6Amroz2CDlea/H7zVDv59fjynhAx0GvoUifCT3GqWg7a\nIAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:25:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDA5NzQ3Nzk1Y2JiNWZjZDI2NzkxOTVmMzRmZWRlZjFiZGU1NWQ5MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b","sha":"9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b"}],"sha":"09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/09747795cbb5fcd2679195f34fedef1bde55d90a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:17:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:17:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: wrap event handlers with untrack() to prevent Solid.js reactive loops\n\nThe real root cause: event handlers were running inside Solid''s reactive\ncontext and triggering infinite runUpdates/completeUpdates loops.\n\nThe logs revealed:\n- Only ONE event was emitted (no recursive emissions)\n- The handler executed ONCE\n- But INSIDE the handler, Solid.js went into infinite reactive loop\n- runUpdates → completeUpdates → runUpdates → completeUpdates...\n\nThe fix:\n- Wrapped all VisualFeedbackEventBus handlers in BuilderContext with untrack()\n- untrack() prevents Solid from tracking reactive dependencies inside handlers\n- This breaks the infinite Solid.js reactive loop\n\nChanges:\n- apps/dev/src/context/BuilderContext.tsx: wrapped all 4 event handlers\n  - property:hover handler\n  - property:unhover handler\n  - property:edit:start handler (the problematic one)\n  - property:edit:end handler\n- Removed debug logging from VisualFeedbackEventBus.ts\n\nThis should finally fix the stack overflow!","tree":{"sha":"841e3d73379b4c5c76539f2c66fdb996b8e6dfe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/841e3d73379b4c5c76539f2c66fdb996b8e6dfe4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDliODdhODk5OWZkNTdjMTI4YjNkYTBlMDRiNTNjZjM1OGFjNGJjN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/20462643f846e2a8b0115e90088522b25484554f","sha":"20462643f846e2a8b0115e90088522b25484554f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/20462643f846e2a8b0115e90088522b25484554f"}],"sha":"9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/9b87a8999fd57c128b3da0e04b53cf358ac4bc7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:15:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T12:15:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(ui): add BorderEditor component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: BorderEditor complete\n\nCreated comprehensive BorderEditor component with:\n1. Border width control (using CSSValueInput)\n2. Border style dropdown (all 9 CSS border styles):\n   - Basic: none, solid, dashed, dotted, double\n   - 3D: groove, ridge, inset, outset\n3. Border color picker integration\n4. Toggleable border radius section with:\n   - 4 independent corner inputs (topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft)\n   - Link/unlink toggle for synchronized editing\n   - Collapsed summary display (shows unified or individual values)\n   - Visual link icon (chain link when linked, broken link when unlinked)\n5. Grid layout for 4 corners (2x2)\n6. Disabled state support\n7. SCSS module styling with CSS variables\n\nFeatures:\n- Linked mode: Changing one corner updates all 4\n- Unlinked mode: Independent corner control\n- Smart summary: Shows \"4px\" if all same, or \"4px 2px 4px 2px\" if different\n- Uses ToggleableSection for collapsible radius UI\n- Uses ColorPicker for border color\n- Uses CSSValueInput for all measurements\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/BorderEditor/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- CSSValue Editor ✓\n- ToggleableSection ✓\n- ColorPicker ✓\n- LinkedInputs (for future integration) ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for all components.\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.1 (Border System)","tree":{"sha":"4726f63dfcbf08de2c97fe63186b9ca683261bdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/4726f63dfcbf08de2c97fe63186b9ca683261bdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/5beb087adbeca36315ef7680b6d389cef168d86a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4726f63dfcbf08de2c97fe63186b9ca683261bdc\nparent e944f093c56888305c357d30c1e5efb952cc569b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762949757 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762949757 +0000\n\nfeat(ui): add BorderEditor component for feature parity\n\nPHASE 0A - Common Systems: BorderEditor complete\n\nCreated comprehensive BorderEditor component with:\n1. Border width control (using CSSValueInput)\n2. Border style dropdown (all 9 CSS border styles):\n   - Basic: none, solid, dashed, dotted, double\n   - 3D: groove, ridge, inset, outset\n3. Border color picker integration\n4. Toggleable border radius section with:\n   - 4 independent corner inputs (topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft)\n   - Link/unlink toggle for synchronized editing\n   - Collapsed summary display (shows unified or individual values)\n   - Visual link icon (chain link when linked, broken link when unlinked)\n5. Grid layout for 4 corners (2x2)\n6. Disabled state support\n7. SCSS module styling with CSS variables\n\nFeatures:\n- Linked mode: Changing one corner updates all 4\n- Unlinked mode: Independent corner control\n- Smart summary: Shows \"4px\" if all same, or \"4px 2px 4px 2px\" if different\n- Uses ToggleableSection for collapsible radius UI\n- Uses ColorPicker for border color\n- Uses CSSValueInput for all measurements\n\nLocated: packages/ui-solid/src/molecules/BorderEditor/\nExported from molecules index\n\nDependencies satisfied:\n- CSSValue Editor ✓\n- ToggleableSection ✓\n- ColorPicker ✓\n- LinkedInputs (for future integration) ✓\n\nReady for integration into PropertyPanel for all components.\n\nRef: REQUIREMENTS.md Section 20.2.1 (Border System)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGBxlQaz\nX6spguNg9ddpEH1/h1UiStzkBxAg5qytH9ki5EgyomrJA3ZGmwsnjBJj6oU6ymZqTavZunYmpEgm\nQgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-12T12:16:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https: