8a093e52d7","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKGEwMjlkNTUyMDA0N2RlYTBmYjRlYjBiYzFlNTY4MDhhMDkzZTUyZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/662eb5383a271ae5a650b9f27ca9f955ff28bbf6","sha":"662eb5383a271ae5a650b9f27ca9f955ff28bbf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/662eb5383a271ae5a650b9f27ca9f955ff28bbf6"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/5ba418a509636e5bc1245f0bd849f519f7ad01e8","sha":"5ba418a509636e5bc1245f0bd849f519f7ad01e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/5ba418a509636e5bc1245f0bd849f519f7ad01e8"}],"sha":"a029d5520047dea0fb4eb0bc1e56808a093e52d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/a029d5520047dea0fb4eb0bc1e56808a093e52d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/662eb5383a271ae5a650b9f27ca9f955ff28bbf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T08:50:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T08:50:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: add comprehensive testing, documentation, and linting for async event bus\n\nImplemented all three remaining items from PR review questions:\n\n1. Unit Tests\n   - Created comprehensive test suite for VisualFeedbackEventBus\n   - 21 tests covering all functionality and async behavior\n   - Specific tests for Solid.js recursion prevention\n   - Tests for re-entry, rapid emissions, and error handling\n   - All tests passing ✅\n\n2. Architecture Documentation\n   - Created async-event-bus-pattern.md in docs/architecture\n   - Comprehensive guide covering pattern definition, rationale, and usage\n   - Comparison of deferral methods (queueMicrotask, Promise, setTimeout)\n   - Implementation checklist and code review guidelines\n   - Migration guide and alternatives analysis\n   - Real-world examples from VisualFeedbackEventBus\n\n3. ESLint Rule\n   - Created custom ESLint plugin (eslint-plugin-local)\n   - Rule: no-sync-event-emit-in-handlers\n   - Detects synchronous event emission in:\n     * DOM event handlers (onClick, onFocus, etc.)\n     * Reactive effects (createEffect, useEffect, etc.)\n   - Allows async wrappers (queueMicrotask, setTimeout, Promise)\n   - Configured as \"warn\" in root .eslintrc.json\n\nThis establishes the async event bus pattern as the standard for the\nproject and provides tooling to prevent future recursion issues.\n\nFiles Added:\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.test.ts\n- docs/architecture/async-event-bus-pattern.md\n- eslint-plugin-local/index.js\n- eslint-plugin-local/rules/no-sync-event-emit-in-handlers.js\n- eslint-plugin-local/README.md\n\nFiles Modified:\n- .eslintrc.json (added local plugin and rule)","tree":{"sha":"5e846aa840b6d8fb8312276495badc756b6601a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/5e846aa840b6d8fb8312276495badc756b6601a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/662eb5383a271ae5a650b9f27ca9f955ff28bbf6","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e846aa840b6d8fb8312276495badc756b6601a2\nparent 9cb817ba4220dfce69154bc86ca31b0949206cbe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762937425 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762937444 +0000\n\nfeat: add comprehensive testing, documentation, and linting for async event bus\n\nImplemented all three remaining items from PR review questions:\n\n1. Unit Tests\n   - Created comprehensive test suite for VisualFeedbackEventBus\n   - 21 tests covering all functionality and async behavior\n   - Specific tests for Solid.js recursion prevention\n   - Tests for re-entry, rapid emissions, and error handling\n   - All tests passing ✅\n\n2. Architecture Documentation\n   - Created async-event-bus-pattern.md in docs/architecture\n   - Comprehensive guide covering pattern definition, rationale, and usage\n   - Comparison of deferral methods (queueMicrotask, Promise, setTimeout)\n   - Implementation checklist and code review guidelines\n   - Migration guide and alternatives analysis\n   - Real-world examples from VisualFeedbackEventBus\n\n3. ESLint Rule\n   - Created custom ESLint plugin (eslint-plugin-local)\n   - Rule: no-sync-event-emit-in-handlers\n   - Detects synchronous event emission in:\n     * DOM event handlers (onClick, onFocus, etc.)\n     * Reactive effects (createEffect, useEffect, etc.)\n   - Allows async wrappers (queueMicrotask, setTimeout, Promise)\n   - Configured as \"warn\" in root .eslintrc.json\n\nThis establishes the async event bus pattern as the standard for the\nproject and provides tooling to prevent future recursion issues.\n\nFiles Added:\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.test.ts\n- docs/architecture/async-event-bus-pattern.md\n- eslint-plugin-local/index.js\n- eslint-plugin-local/rules/no-sync-event-emit-in-handlers.js\n- eslint-plugin-local/README.md\n\nFiles Modified:\n- .eslintrc.json (added local plugin and rule)\n","reason":"va