:19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/3c41866384a372de024dff89de4757c2ca282852","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDNjNDE4NjYzODRhMzcyZGUwMjRkZmY4OWRlNDc1N2MyY2EyODI4NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791","sha":"a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701","sha":"3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701"}],"sha":"3c41866384a372de024dff89de4757c2ca282852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/3c41866384a372de024dff89de4757c2ca282852"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-11T11:59:01Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-11T11:59:01Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: introduce createBEM utility for intuitive BEM class name access\n\nThis commit introduces a new `createBEM` factory function that provides a more\nintuitive and maintainable way to work with BEM class names in CSS Modules.\n\n## Changes\n\n### New Utility Function\n- Added `createBEM(styles, block)` function to `classNames.ts`\n- Returns a BEM helper with methods for accessing block, element, and modifier classes\n- Provides explicit API: `bem()`, `bem(modifier)`, `bem.elem(element)`, `bem.elem(element, modifier)`\n\n### Updated Documentation\n- Enhanced `CSS_MODULES_GUIDE.md` with createBEM examples and best practices\n- Added migration guide for transitioning from getStyleClass to createBEM\n- Documented all API methods and usage patterns\n\n### Component Migrations\n- **ui-solid components**: Migrated atoms (Button, Icon, Input, Label) and Modal to use createBEM\n- **ui-components classes**: Migrated all core components to use createBEM pattern:\n  - Atoms: Button, Icon, Input, Label\n  - Molecules: Alert, Dropdown, Modal, Tabs\n\n## Benefits\n- **DRY**: Define styles and block name once, reuse throughout component\n- **Readable**: `bem(''open'')` is clearer than `getStyleClass(styles, ''modal--open'')`\n- **Maintainable**: Enforces proper BEM naming structure\n- **Type-safe**: Better TypeScript support for class name access\n- **Consistent**: Standardized approach across all UI components\n\n## API Examples\n```typescript\nconst bem = createBEM(styles, ''modal'');\nbem()                    // → modal\nbem(''open'')              // → modal--open\nbem.elem(''dialog'')       // → modal__dialog\nbem.elem(''close'', ''disabled'') // → modal__close--disabled\n```\n\nAll changes are backwards compatible - existing getStyleClass calls continue to work.","tree":{"sha":"a034c0589a094f0e1a94920c726f47e4d4da62d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/a034c0589a094f0e1a94920c726f47e4d4da62d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701","verification":{"payload":"tree a034c0589a094f0e1a94920c726f47e4d4da62d2\nparent a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762862341 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762862341 +0000\n\nfeat: introduce createBEM utility for intuitive BEM class name access\n\nThis commit introduces a new `createBEM` factory function that provides a more\nintuitive and maintainable way to work with BEM class names in CSS Modules.\n\n## Changes\n\n### New Utility Function\n- Added `createBEM(styles, block)` function to `classNames.ts`\n- Returns a BEM helper with methods for accessing block, element, and modifier classes\n- Provides explicit API: `bem()`, `bem(modifier)`, `bem.elem(element)`, `bem.elem(element, modifier)`\n\n### Updated Documentation\n- Enhanced `CSS_MODULES_GUIDE.md` with createBEM examples and best practices\n- Added migration guide for transitioning from getStyleClass to createBEM\n- Documented all API methods and usage patterns\n\n### Component Migrations\n- **ui-solid components**: Migrated atoms (Button, Icon, Input, Label) and Modal to use createBEM\n- **ui-components classes**: Migrated all core components to use createBEM pattern:\n  - Atoms: Button, Icon, Input, Label\n  - Molecules: Alert, Dropdown, Modal, Tabs\n\n## Benefits\n- **DRY**: Define styles and block name once, reuse throughout component\n- **Readable**: `bem(''open'')` is clearer than `getStyleClass(styles, ''modal--open'')`\n- **Maintainable**: Enforces proper BEM naming structure\n- **Type-safe**: Better TypeScript support for class name access\n- **Consistent**: Standardized approach across all UI components\n\n## API Examples\n```typescript\nconst bem = createBEM(styles, ''modal'');\nbem()                    // → modal\nbem(''open'')              // → modal--open\nbem.elem(''dialog'')       // → modal__dialog\nbem.elem(''close'', ''disabled'') // → modal__close--disabled\n```\n\nAll changes are backwards compatible - existing getStyleClass calls continue to work.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJg2Q8lm\nbVuxyqsmu3T5lSKR92Q+1JgNW9Nm/uEdWWPjvhpOAOWa/gogI2PLFOEzcvZlrYYLm7VbS9QknOJ2\ndw4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-11T11:59:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDNmODZhNjc3ZjgzNDczMzUxMzA2NDgxZDUxNjM2ZDgwODQ0M2Q3MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791","sha":"a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/a2db9defaf0df6ab0a933f7c222410956cecd791"}],"sha":"3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/3f86a677f83473351306481d51636d808443d701"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commits/188fd150a55e9d0b2bd0a3ef6aa39924cdbfa7ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-11T11:55:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-11T11:55:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor: implement event bus for visual feedback to fix infinite recursion\n\nThis is a complete refactor of the visual feedback system to fix the\ninfinite recursion issue using a global event bus pattern instead of\ncomponent props.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe infinite recursion was caused by handler functions being recreated\non every render, causing PropertyPanel to receive new props and re-render\ncontinuously. This created a feedback loop when focus events triggered\nstate updates in Builder.tsx.\n\n## Solution: Global Event Bus\nImplemented a singleton event bus (VisualFeedbackEventBus) that completely\ndecouples visual feedback events from the component prop chain:\n\n1. PropertyPanel emits events to the global bus\n2. BuilderContext subscribes to events and forwards to VisualFeedbackManager\n3. Builder.tsx subscribes for accessibility state updates only\n4. No props passing = no re-render loops\n\n## Changes\n\n### New File: packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.ts\n- Created singleton event bus for visual feedback events\n- Supports: property:hover, property:unhover, property:edit:start, property:edit:end\n- Provides subscribe/unsubscribe functionality with cleanup\n\n### Modified: packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.tsx\n- Removed all visualFeedback prop dependencies\n- Changed handlers to emit events to global bus\n- Simplified event handlers (no more untrack, queueMicrotask)\n- Removed recursive call guards (no longer needed)\n\n### Modified: apps/dev/src/context/BuilderContext.tsx\n- Added event bus subscriptions in visual feedback manager setup\n- Removed old onPropertyHover, onPropertyUnhover, onPropertyEditStart, onPropertyEditEnd actions\n- Event handlers now live in createEffect with proper cleanup\n\n### Modified: apps/dev/src/pages/Builder.tsx\n- Removed visualFeedback prop to PropertyPanel\n- Added event bus subscriptions for accessibility updates only\n- Simplified accessibility state management\n- Removed complex handler memoization\n\n### Modified: packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.types.ts\n- Removed visualFeedback from PropertyPanelProps interface\n- Removed PropertyHoverEvent and PropertyEditEvent exports (moved to event bus)\n\n## Benefits\n- ✅ Fixes infinite recursion completely\n- ✅ Visual feedback system fully functional\n- ✅ Cleaner separation of concerns\n- ✅ No prop drilling\n- ✅ Easier to test and debug\n- ✅ Better performance (no unnecessary re-renders)\n\n## Testing\nTest by:\n1. Create new template\n2. Drag button component\n3. Switch to style tab\n4. Click border radius input\n5. Verify no stack overflow error\n6. Hover over inputs to see visual feedback working\n\nRelated files:\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.ts (new)\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/index.ts\n- packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.tsx\n- packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.types.ts\n- apps/dev/src/context/BuilderContext.tsx\n- apps/dev/src/pages/Builder.tsx","tree":{"sha":"d9fe9e1b209de4948002cc65d9fd478e783d5a9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/trees/d9fe9e1b209de4948002cc65d9fd478e783d5a9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/git/commits/188fd150a55e9d0b2bd0a3ef6aa39924cdbfa7ed","verification":{"payload":"tree d9fe9e1b209de4948002cc65d9fd478e783d5a9d\nparent 6c9f4e9d34f1ecc4d493e9c1f1648dbf545811e6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762862110 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762862110 +0000\n\nrefactor: implement event bus for visual feedback to fix infinite recursion\n\nThis is a complete refactor of the visual feedback system to fix the\ninfinite recursion issue using a global event bus pattern instead of\ncomponent props.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe infinite recursion was caused by handler functions being recreated\non every render, causing PropertyPanel to receive new props and re-render\ncontinuously. This created a feedback loop when focus events triggered\nstate updates in Builder.tsx.\n\n## Solution: Global Event Bus\nImplemented a singleton event bus (VisualFeedbackEventBus) that completely\ndecouples visual feedback events from the component prop chain:\n\n1. PropertyPanel emits events to the global bus\n2. BuilderContext subscribes to events and forwards to VisualFeedbackManager\n3. Builder.tsx subscribes for accessibility state updates only\n4. No props passing = no re-render loops\n\n## Changes\n\n### New File: packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.ts\n- Created singleton event bus for visual feedback events\n- Supports: property:hover, property:unhover, property:edit:start, property:edit:end\n- Provides subscribe/unsubscribe functionality with cleanup\n\n### Modified: packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.tsx\n- Removed all visualFeedback prop dependencies\n- Changed handlers to emit events to global bus\n- Simplified event handlers (no more untrack, queueMicrotask)\n- Removed recursive call guards (no longer needed)\n\n### Modified: apps/dev/src/context/BuilderContext.tsx\n- Added event bus subscriptions in visual feedback manager setup\n- Removed old onPropertyHover, onPropertyUnhover, onPropertyEditStart, onPropertyEditEnd actions\n- Event handlers now live in createEffect with proper cleanup\n\n### Modified: apps/dev/src/pages/Builder.tsx\n- Removed visualFeedback prop to PropertyPanel\n- Added event bus subscriptions for accessibility updates only\n- Simplified accessibility state management\n- Removed complex handler memoization\n\n### Modified: packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.types.ts\n- Removed visualFeedback from PropertyPanelProps interface\n- Removed PropertyHoverEvent and PropertyEditEvent exports (moved to event bus)\n\n## Benefits\n- ✅ Fixes infinite recursion completely\n- ✅ Visual feedback system fully functional\n- ✅ Cleaner separation of concerns\n- ✅ No prop drilling\n- ✅ Easier to test and debug\n- ✅ Better performance (no unnecessary re-renders)\n\n## Testing\nTest by:\n1. Create new template\n2. Drag button component\n3. Switch to style tab\n4. Click border radius input\n5. Verify no stack overflow error\n6. Hover over inputs to see visual feedback working\n\nRelated files:\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/VisualFeedbackEventBus.ts (new)\n- packages/core/visual-feedback/index.ts\n- packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.tsx\n- packages/ui-solid/src/sidebar/PropertyPanel.types.ts\n- apps/dev/src/context/BuilderContext.tsx\n- apps/dev/src/pages/Builder.tsx\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOvOr5ZC\nTTmraS6B2UNyvGaC4uoBJ7gdL2uHdS3QGdTfj0JdLRKUPmfYuL90OdTFLIQdcqqe2aTeYtlysxqt\noQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-11T11:55:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rmadeiraneto/email-builder/commit/188fd150a55e9d0b2bd0a3ef6aa39924cdbfa7ed","node_id":"C_kwDOQLsh1NoAKDE4OGZkMTUwYTU1ZTlkMGIyYmQwYTNlZjZhYTM5OTI0Y2RiZmE3ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"